        "original_id": "ea5f21d9-ec52-51ff-86cb-f615025fe221",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Products: Texas Raiders, Boeing B-17 Flying Fortress, B-17G-95-DL\n- Organizations: General Aviation Services, United States Army Air Corps\n- Places: Conroe North Houston Regional Airport, Conroe, Texas\n- Topics: bomber development, aircraft production\n\nFacts:\n- The Boeing B-17 Flying Fortress was developed in the 1930s as a four-engine heavy bomber for the United States Army Air Corps.\n- The Boeing B-17 Flying Fortress was introduced in 1938 and later evolved through numerous design advances.\n- The Boeing B-17 Flying Fortress became the third-most produced bomber of all time, behind the Consolidated B-24 Liberator and the Junkers Ju 88.\n- Texas Raiders is an American Boeing B-17 Flying Fortress of the Douglas-Long Beach built B-17G-95-DL variant.\n- Texas Raiders is hangared at General Aviation Services at Conroe North Houston Regional Airport in Conroe, Texas.",
